{"name":"Courtly Purple","hex":"#bbafc1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"courtly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Befitting of a royal court; reflecting the manners or behaviour of people at court; stately, rich or fine, and so suitable for a royal court.","Of or relating to courtly love or courtship."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In the manner of a royal court; in a manner befitting of a royal court."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/courtly"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Courtesy","blocks":[{"text":"Courtesy is gentle politeness and courtly manners. In the Middle Ages in Europe, the behaviour expected of the nobility was compiled in courtesy books."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Courtesy_Call.jpg/330px-Courtesy_Call.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Courtesy"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Ghent_Altarpiece_D_-_Popes_-_Bishops.jpg/500px-Ghent_Altarpiece_D_-_Popes_-_Bishops.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Ghent_Altarpiece_D_-_Popes_-_Bishops.jpg/500px-Ghent_Altarpiece_D_-_Popes_-_Bishops.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGhent_Altarpiece_D_-_Popes_-_Bishops.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/M81.jpg/500px-M81.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/M81.jpg/500px-M81.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AM81.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Segmented_aubergine_Thailand.jpg/500px-Segmented_aubergine_Thailand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Segmented_aubergine_Thailand.jpg/500px-Segmented_aubergine_Thailand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASegmented_aubergine_Thailand.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Auke_Bay_Alaska_2.jpg/500px-Auke_Bay_Alaska_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/